A||||3||Ironhorse||Lumina Tranny||||1||
Z||000000||Ironhorse||11-12-2000||01:55 AM||||Hey there Fieroholics, My dad has a 1990 chev lumina with alumium 3.1 and a auto tranny. He said that he will give me the transmission if it will fit.. I told him that I'm almost postiive that it will fit.  I did some check up and got confuse.  There seem to be 2 type of Tranny for this car.  A TH125 tranny, and a TH-440-T4 (4T60) tranny.. I'm not sure which is which and what the difference between those.  The kickdown cable, shifting cable, and TC plugs look same but looks can be deciving.  Exactly how do I find out?  Even if it's TH 440, will it still hook up to 85 2.8 engine?  TIA ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-12-2000||08:03 AM||||The th125c is a three speed. The th440t4 is a four speed. Either one will bolt to the 2.8 but the 440t4 will require different axles and modified mounts.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ironhorse||11-12-2000||04:48 PM||||Great, thanks for information.  How or where do I need to look for on what type of transmission it is.  If it's a TH440 tranny, how much of a modification is it to install it?  Can I use the axle from the 90 lumina and put it in the fiero along with the TH440 tranny?||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||11-12-2000||07:25 PM||||If it's a 440t4, it will have PRND321 on the shift indicator (the D might be an O). If it's a th125 it will have PRND21. Do as search of the forum for things like TH440T4, 440T4, 4T60, 4T60E, four speed auto, etc.. There has been much discussion about what is required to do the swap. The TH440T4 is the same thing as a 4T60, and the 4T60E is the electronic version that was introduced in 90 or 91. The Lumina axles will most likely be too long. It has been said that Transport/APV/Silloette axles with Fiero outer CV joints fit a 4T60 Fiero. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
